WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.430
Sometimes you just need a few extra seconds
before all the screaming and stabbing starts

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.000
up again.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.660
From nightmarish jump scares to unbelievably
weird-looking beasts, these are the most paused

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.020
horror movie moments.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.140
David Kessler is having a rough vacation.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.520
He just wanted to go backpacking across the
Yorkshire moors, but the moment he steps off

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.910
the beaten path, he's attacked by a werewolf.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.320
When he wakes up in a London hospital, he
keeps having ghastly nightmares.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.780
These freaky dreams are the scariest parts
of An American Werewolf in London.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.000
From the hospital, we cut to David's home.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.460
He's working on his college homework, his
family is watching TV, and everything seems

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.240
peaceful.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.219
Before we can get our bearings, an army of
mutant Nazi monsters bursts into the house

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.000
and guns down David's family.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.140
They burn his home, shoot everything to pieces,
and kill David.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.020
And that's when our hero wakes up in his hospital
bed.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.480
It was all just a nasty Nazi dream, and his
sympathetic nurse is only too happy to open

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.340
up the curtains and let some sunlight in.

00:01:00.569 --> 00:01:06.000
But as she pulls back the shades, there's
a Nazi-Beast standing there, knife in hand,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.680
and he stabs the nurse to death.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.170
We haven't even seen the American werewolf
yet, and we're already pressing pause so we

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.509
can collect our nerves.

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:20.020
The psycho witch turned evil spirit, Bathsheba
is having a great time in The Conjuring, terrorizing

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.540
the poor Perron family.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.820
Of course, if those kids think they're scared
whenever Bathsheba shows up, then they've

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.780
got no idea what we're going through.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:33.000
Whether she's playing "hide and clap" in the
cellar or getting all possessive, every time

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.200
this hag shows up on screen, we're hiding
behind the sofa.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.800
Of course, there's one Bathsheba scene that
stands head and shoulders above the rest.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.600
It's the scene where young Andrea hears something
banging around inside her wardrobe.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.140
Nervous, she goes to check it out, flings
open the doors, and finds nothing inside.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.800
That's because Bathsheba is up on top, just
waiting to pounce.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:59.960
Horror fans will want to press the pause button
here for multiple reasons.

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:05.679
One, it's our first good look at the demon
haunting the Perron family, and she is a terrifying

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:06.500
sight to behold.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.390
Secondly, this is one of the scariest scenes
in movie history, and when your heart rate

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.570
spikes to new and dangerous levels, you'll
need to take a break and remind yourself it's

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:16.280
just a movie.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:22.180
Wes Craven and Sam Raimi are masters of the
horror genre, and their films have a combined

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.460
body count higher than most serial killers.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:29.240
In addition to giving us some of the scariest
movies ever made, Craven and Raimi also had

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:34.240
a friendly feud going on, where they'd reference
each other's movies in their own films.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.960
For example, in the first Evil Dead, a slashed-up
movie poster for The Hills Have Eyes makes

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.540
an appearance.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:45.400
Craven returned the favor in A Nightmare on
Elm Street when Nancy Thompson falls asleep

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.640
watching Evil Dead.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:52.000
Raimi's well-loved film makes another appearance
in the Craven-directed Scream, when one character

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.920
considers watching the undead action flick
before deciding against it.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.860
"How many Evil Dead?

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.220
How many Hellraiser?"

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:06.320
As for Raimi, he absolutely loves putting
Freddy Krueger's glove into his deadite franchise.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:11.560
Not only did it show up in an episode of Ash
vs. Evil Dead, but the deadly fashion accessory

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.400
also appears in Raimi's horror masterpiece,
Evil Dead II.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.400
Eagle-eyed horror fans should press pause
when Ash Williams heads down into the fruit

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.700
cellar or walks into the woodshed.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.780
The glove shows up in both scenes, hanging
on the wall in all its razor-bladed glory.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:34.500
Now we can't stop thinking about that Freddy
vs. Jason vs. Ash movie that we're never going

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.000
to get.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.460
The Stephen King bestseller Gerald's Game
seems like an unfilmable book.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.240
The plot follows a woman named Jessie who
retreats to a secluded country house with

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.380
her husband Gerald, where they hope to rekindle
their marriage.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.920
Unfortunately, after cuffing his wife to the
bed, Gerald keels over from a heart attack,

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.300
leaving his wife handcuffed to the bed alone.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:00.000
From there, the novel pretty much takes place
inside Jessie's head.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:05.560
Somehow, director Mike Flanagan and actress
Carla Gugino turned this crazy book into one

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.060
of the very best King adaptations.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.220
Of course, that also means they had to shoot
the infamous degloving scene.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:13.700
"Okay then.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.240
Visualize it then.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:17.720
All of it."

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:22.680
Now, there are horror moments that make you
scream, and ones that make you want to throw

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.180
up.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.480
The degloving scene from Gerald's Game will
make you want to do both at once.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.960
Desperate to get free, especially since a
hungry dog and the creepy Moonlight Man might

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.980
return any time, Jessie takes some serious
steps to escape her bonds.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.940
She slits her wrist with a piece of glass
and then she just starts yanking until the

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.400
skin on her hand starts peeling off.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.940
She basically turns her hand inside out to
make her great escape.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.120
This gnarly scene sent people into hysterics,
and once it's all over, the pause button will

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.860
come in handy as you proceed to lose your
lunch.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.960
It is full of blink-and-you'll-miss-it moments
that require a pause button to fully appreciate,

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:06.500
like the scene when Ben Hanscom spends a day
studying at the library.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.040
Unfortunately, things take an unsettling turn
when a librarian shows up.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.460
When she hands Ben a book on local history,
she shames him for staying indoors during

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.090
the summer, but Ben just ignores her.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.100
"A boy should be spending his summer with
friends.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.740
Don't you have any friends?"

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:26.740
"Can I have the book now?"

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.940
However, reading about Derry isn't a relaxing
way to spend your day.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:37.340
The town has a haunted history, and Ben is
horrified to learn about a devastating explosion

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:41.080
that decapitated some poor kid and sent his
head hurling into a tree.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.200
The images are upsetting, but the really scary
stuff is happening behind Ben.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:51.580
After the librarian leaves, another librarian,
who was previously shelving volumes in the

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.450
background before the conversation, stops
what she's doing and starts staring at Ben

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:00.120
- just before Pennywise starts appearing in
the book's pages.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:04.920
Press pause, and you'll see she's grinning
an evil grin and watching like a predator

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.540
about to devour its prey.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:13.020
Obviously, this means that Pennywise is prowling
about, and the longer you look, the more goosebumps

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:13.560
you get.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:20.820
Mandy is an LSD-infused nightmare, complete
with tigers, chainsaw battles, and a posse

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.280
of demon bikers who look like they just rode
out of Hellraiser.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:28.600
They're known as the Black Skulls, and they
only love two things in this world: drugs

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:29.160
and pain.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:34.000
There are legends of these guys riding up
and down the interstate, murdering truckers

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:38.430
and hitchhikers, and these creatures share
a weird connection with a psycho cult called

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.940
the Children of Dawn.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:45.400
If these hippies ever need some muscle, they
just blow a magical horn and the demons appear,

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.200
ready to ride.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.320
The first time the Black Skulls roll onto
the screen, shrouded by smoke and blood red

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.660
light, it's a moment to behold.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.320
Much like the Cenobites, the Black Skulls
each have their own grotesque look.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:01.900
The design for each biker is so unique that
we've got to press pause and marvel at each

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:07.020
one for just a moment… before they're unleashed
on our poor heroes, and things get gory.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:12.640
The Perfection follows two cellists who both
attended the same prestigious conservatory.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.840
After meeting for the first time, they go
on a roadtrip across China.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.760
However, icky stuff starts happening the moment
they get on the road.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.460
Current superstar Lizzie comes down with a
mysterious flu, and her new friend and lover

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.490
Charlotte does her best to help Lizzie survive
their nightmarish bus trip.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:33.640
As they wind deeper and deeper into the Chinese
mountains, Lizzie starts throwing up all over

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.140
the place.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:39.120
Puking is bad enough, but when Charlotte takes
a closer look, she sees that Lizzie's vomit

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.540
is full of maggots.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:45.220
Even worse, Lizzie's arm starts wriggling,
like insects are literally crawling under

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:45.860
her skin.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:50.820
It looks like she's become some sort of bug
incubator, and the insects are going to devour

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:56.110
her arm… until Charlotte pulls a meat cleaver
out of her backpack and tells Lizzie to chop

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:56.920
off a limb.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:01.600
When Lizzie pulls out that meat cleaver, we've
got to hit pause so we can figure out what

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.680
the heck is going on.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.580
But hey, don't worry, things are going to
get way more bizarre before this film is over.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.699
"Should we just get this check and pretend
that none of this ever happened?"

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:11.500
"This is your moment.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.280
You can bow out gracefully and I'll never
hold it against you."

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:19.979
The Ritual follows four friends who head into
the Swedish woods and encounter a pagan cult

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.740
that worships an ancient entity.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.980
As it turns out, that entity really loves
skewering people on tree branches.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:31.220
The monster is called the Jötunn, a beast
out of Norse mythology, and for most of the

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.700
film, the giant creature keeps out of sight.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:38.620
It hides in the forest, plaguing our four
heroes with horrible nightmares before turning

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.840
them into shish kebabs.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:44.720
Eventually, the surviving backpackers are
captured by that aforementioned cult, and

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:47.480
unlucky Dom is offered to the Jötunn as a
sacrifice.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:52.520
Up until this point, we still haven't seen
the mysterious beast, but when Dom finally

00:08:52.529 --> 00:08:57.120
finds himself face-to-face with the oversized
creature, it's unlike anything we've ever

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.000
seen before.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.500
The Jötunn has the body of a goat on steroids.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:06.660
The top half of its head looks like a decapitated
human torso with deer antlers.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:11.709
Its glowing eyes are buried in a cavern where
its face should be, and there are long human-like

00:09:11.709 --> 00:09:13.820
arms hanging off the sides of its head.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:19.160
It's a truly bizarre creature, and we just
have to press pause and admire its wild design.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:25.020
Unpopular ending aside, Signs is an entertaining
and terrifying sci-fi flick, and there are

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:29.000
more than a few scenes in this M. Night Shyamalan
film that scared us senseless.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:33.839
But if we're talking about pause-worthy moments,
we all know exactly what scene is going to

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.579
make this list: the Brazilian birthday party.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.639
By this point in the film, it's pretty clear
that aliens are invading Earth.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.860
We've got crop circles, lights in the sky,
and chattering voices on baby monitors.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:50.820
But other than a quick glimpse of a leg, we
haven't actually seen an alien yet.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.920
That all changes when Merrill turns on the
news.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:58.180
Not wanting to freak out his family, he moves
the television into a coat closet to follow

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.520
the invasion on the news.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:03.680
When he sees a home video of a close encounter,
Merrill loses his mind.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.600
The footage is shot on a camcorder, lending
a disturbing realism to the scene.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:12.819
A Brazilian dad is filming his kid's birthday
party, but the children are screaming and

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.820
crying because there's something awful outside.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:20.440
The dad points his camera into an alleyway,
and suddenly, the alien lurches into view.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:25.480
The long-limbed creature is only onscreen
for a second, but it's enough to send shivers

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:26.460
down our spines.

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:31.220
We're pressing pause as fast we can because
we need to collect ourselves and to get a

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:33.280
better look at this ugly extraterrestrial.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.760
Home invasion movies might be the scariest
sort of horror movie.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.980
After all, while Freddy Krueger won't actually
kill you in your dreams, it's possible that

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:48.200
a trio of real-world mask-wearing psychos
might drop by one night to terrorize you just

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:48.940
because you're home.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:53.840
That's the premise of The Strangers, a chilling
horror flick where a couple are having one

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.700
tough night even before the Strangers arrive.

00:10:57.129 --> 00:11:00.959
When her boyfriend runs to the store, Kristen
finds herself home alone and feeling a little

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:01.680
unsettled.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:07.740
The house is eerily quiet and strangely empty,
and something feels a little off, almost like

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.520
Kristen is being watched.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.540
And that's because there's a masked killer
standing in the hallway, just a few feet behind

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:14.040
her.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:18.560
The villain stands in the door, perfectly
happy to watch Kristen walk around the house,

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.900
tracking her as she moves from one side of
the room to the other.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:26.990
The whole thing is done in one wide shot,
which creates an unbearable sense of anxiety.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:31.800
The tension is so thick you could cut it with
a knife, and things get so quietly intense

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.019
that we can't help but press pause.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.060
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:40.860
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
horror movies are coming soon.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:44.560
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

